-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Cisco Heat
  Publisher   Image Works, 1991
  Version     1.2

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Ciscoheat.tap
  MD5         7cf4c47830a587bb0d79fbbc72bb0992

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Pace        original

  Changes     1.2: the player's car is solid: road lines, posts and other cars
              behind it no longer show through it (the original draws it with
              no mask; inside its outline the road's own colour shows, as in
              the original where nothing is behind it). 1.1: keeps the CPU
              speed you choose (the start set 3.5 MHz) and starts with the
              Next's DivMMC automap switched off (nexclash main, 2026-11-23).
              1.0: first NXC patch, from nexclash cisco_heat v1.2 with no
              loading-screen hold

  Note        Keys as the original. Smooth engine: the game's own update at
              the original pace, with up to 50 in-between pictures a second
              drawn by the game's own code, and the player's car as red Next
              sprites, so road lines, posts and other cars beside it no longer
              turn red. The tape's loading screen shows from ENTER while the
              patch builds and while the game loads; the game then starts at
              once. The five stages are kept in memory: no tape loads between
              stages. Toggles: 25 pictures a second is the v1.1 cadence, more
              even steps; Original picture rate shows one picture per game
              update, as the original; Original car colours draws the car in
              the game's red cells, with the clash. With Original picture rate
              on, 25 pictures a second does nothing. Known issues: pictures
              are unevenly spaced at the 50 cadence (1- and 2-frame steps),
              each at its own in-between position; the car's shadow is black,
              as in the original.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite time

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release (Spectrum Computing,
  ZXDB entry 968). Infinite time holds the whole seconds; the tenths still
  run.

