              (2026-11-23, nexclash main e55537e: v1.2 plus the caller's CPU
              speed kept at the start; same results as 1.0 on the same
              recordings, selftest --verify PASSED) and 1.0 (2026-11-22,
              nexclash cisco_heat v1.2 with no loading-screen hold): the real
              update, run at 28 MHz, against the original 0x8AFE from the same
              state, and the in-between frames (smooth on against off, every
              byte they write put back): 159 cases from six recordings (stages
              1-5 and the end sequence), real update and in-between frames
              IDENTICAL in 159 of 159, 754 in-between frames, none late; 43
              captured states with the car on, every 10th update, IDENTICAL.
              Toggles (each display only): 25 pictures a second, stage 3, 37
              of 37 IDENTICAL, 131 in-between frames; Original car colours
              (the car's cells red as the game makes them, no sprites), stage
              1, 33 of 33 IDENTICAL, 149 in-between frames; Original picture
