              every real-update case above runs. Car sprites: the game's car
              routine on a clear buffer, the sprites inside their clip window
              show exactly the pixels the game makes red, 111 frames, mirrored
              images included.

  Emulator    JNext 1.2.0 headless, the bare build without the hold's loader
              screen (v1.2): game state in lockstep with the original for 300
              updates on two input seeds; AY writes and interrupts as the
              original; flicker, 100 frames: 59 picture changes against the
              original's 11, none out of step, vanished or transient. Not run
              through the real NXC loader.

  Coverage    Stages 1-5 and the end sequence from the owner's recordings. Not
              covered: a full unassisted playthrough; the 25 pictures a second
              and Original car colours toggles on stages other than those
              named; the trainers in JNext or on hardware; joystick.

  Hardware    ZX Spectrum Next (Kickstarter 3), System/Next 26.11a: played by
              the owner, the player's car is solid now; the other cars can
              seem to pass through it (being looked at) (earlier: v1.2 as a
              bare .nex (with the 4 s screen hold) on a Spectrum Next: played
              by the owner, "it works great".)

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
